{"arrivo":"nl","origine":"fro-nor","origine_nome":"Old Northern French","livello2":"LATINO","livello2_nome":"Latin (all varieties)","n":13,"parole":[{"parola":"-esse","pos":"suffix","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"creates the female form of some persons or occupations, as English -ess","termine_origine":"-esse","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"-esse","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"-issa","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-lat","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch -esse, borrowed from Old Northern French -esse, from Late Latin -issa (as in abbātissa (“abbess”)).","livello2_varieta":"la-lat"},{"parola":"abeel","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"abele; term used of certain poplars, mainly the white poplar (Populus alba), grey poplar (Populus × canescens) or black…","termine_origine":"abiel","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"abiel","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"albellus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch abeel, from Old Northern French abiel, from Latin albellus, a diminutive of albus (“white”).","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"canvas","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"canvas, sail","termine_origine":"canevas","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"canevas","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"cannabis","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"κάνναβις","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"canvas","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"en","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch canevas, from Old Northern French canevas, from Latin cannabis, from Ancient Greek κάνναβις (kánnabis). The spelling was lated influenced by English canvas. Doublet of cannabis and hennep.","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"fluwijn","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"synonym of steenmarter (“beech marten (Martes foina)”)","termine_origine":"*floïne","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"*floïne","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"fāgīna (mūstēla)","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch fluwijn, from Old Northern French *floïne (modern Picard floène, flouène), a variant of Old French foïne (modern French fouine), from Latin fāgīna (mūstēla) (“beech weasel”).","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"kabel","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"cable","termine_origine":"cable","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"cable","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"capulum","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-lat","ambiti":["informatica"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch cabel, from Old Northern French cable, a variant of Old French chable, from Late Latin capulum.","livello2_varieta":"la-lat"},{"parola":"kachtel","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"foal","termine_origine":"captel","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"captel","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"capitāle","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-med","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch cachtel, from earlier caftel, from Old Northern French captel, from Medieval Latin capitāle (“young cattle”), from Classical Latin capitālis (“of the head”), from caput (“head”) + -alis (“-al”). Cognate with English cattle.","livello2_varieta":"la-med"},{"parola":"kans","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"chance","termine_origine":"caance","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"caance","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-vul","nome":"Vulgar Latin","termine":"*cadentia","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-vul","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch canse, borrowed from Old Northern French caance (compare central cheance), from Vulgar Latin *cadentia, from cadere (“to fall”), referring to the falling of dice. Doublet of cadans, cadens, and sjans. Cognate with French chance, English chance.","livello2_varieta":"la-vul"},{"parola":"kant","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"side, face (of an object)","termine_origine":"cant","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"cant","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"canthus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-med","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch cant, from Old Northern French cant, from Medieval Latin canthus.","livello2_varieta":"la-med"},{"parola":"karbonkel","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"ruby, garnet","termine_origine":"carbuncle","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"carbuncle","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"carbunculus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":["diritto_politica"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch carbonkel, from Old Northern French carbuncle, from Latin carbunculus.","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"kasteel","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"castle, either palatial or fortified","termine_origine":"castel","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"castel","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"castellum","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":["mare","sport"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch castēel, from Old Northern French castel, from Latin castellum. Doublet of Kessel, chateau, Castilië, castellum, ketella, and telo.","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"klant","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"customer, client","termine_origine":"calant","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"calant","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"caleō","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch calant (“person, friend”), from Old Northern French calant (compare regular Old French chalant), from Old French chaloir (“to heat, to care about”), from Latin caleō (“to be hot”).","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"plank","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"shelf","termine_origine":"planke","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"planke","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"planca","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-lat","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch planke, from Old Dutch *planka, from Old Northern French planke, from Late Latin planca.","livello2_varieta":"la-lat"},{"parola":"schaars","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Of uncertain origin","significato":"scarce","termine_origine":"scars","catena":[{"codice":"fro-nor","nome":"Old Northern French","termine":"scars","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"*scarpsus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-lat","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch schaers. From Old Northern French scars, escars (\"sparing, niggard, parsimonious, miserly, poor\"; > French échars, Medieval Latin scarsus (“diminished, reduced”)), of uncertain origin. One theory is that it derives originally from a Late Latin *scarpsus, *excarpsus, a participle fo","livello2_varieta":"la-lat"}]}